            <node id="42" label="cron">
                <attvalues>
                    <attvalue for="0" value="process scheduling daemon" />
                    <attvalue for="1" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="2" value="process scheduling daemon&#10; The cron daemon is a background process that runs particular programs at&#10; particular times (for example, every minute, day, week, or month), as&#10; specified in a crontab. By default, users may also create crontabs of&#10; their own so that processes are run on their behalf.&#10; .&#10; Output from the commands is usually mailed to the system administrator&#10; (or to the user in question); you should probably install a mail system&#10; as well so that you can receive these messages.&#10; .&#10; This cron package does not provide any system maintenance tasks. Basic&#10; periodic maintenance tasks are provided by other packages, such&#10; as checksecurity." />
                    <attvalue for="3" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="4" value="235" />
                    <attvalue for="5" value="no" />
                    <attvalue for="6" value="Ubuntu Developers &lt;ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com&gt;" />
                    <attvalue for="7" value="" />
                    <attvalue for="8" value='[[{"name": "cron-daemon", "op": null, "version": null}]]' />
                    <attvalue for="9" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="10" value='[[{"name": "bcron", "op": null, "version": null}], [{"name": "cronie", "op": null, "version": null}], [{"name": "systemd-cron", "op": null, "version": null}]]' />
                    <attvalue for="11" value="admin" />
                    <attvalue for="12" value="cron" />
                    <attvalue for="13" value="3.0pl1-200ubuntu1" />
                    <attvalue for="14" value='[[{"name": "anacron", "op": null, "version": null}], [{"name": "logrotate", "op": null, "version": null}], [{"name": "checksecurity", "op": null, "version": null}], [{"name": "supercat", "op": null, "version": null}], [{"name": "bat", "op": null, "version": null}], [{"name": "default-mta", "op": null, "version": null}, {"name": "mail-transport-agent", "op": null, "version": null}]]' />
                    <attvalue for="15" value="3.0pl1-200ubuntu1" />
                </attvalues>
                </node>
            <node id="43" label="cron-daemon-common">
                <attvalues>
                    <attvalue for="0" value="process scheduling daemon's configuration files" />
                    <attvalue for="1" value='[[{"name": "systemd-cron", "op": "&lt;&lt;", "version": "1.15.19-5~"}]]' />
                    <attvalue for="2" value="process scheduling daemon's configuration files&#10; The cron daemon is a background process that runs particular programs at&#10; particular times (for example, every minute, day, week, or month), as&#10; specified in a crontab. By default, users may also create crontabs of&#10; their own so that processes are run on their behalf.&#10; .&#10; This package provides configuration files which must be there to&#10; define scheduled process sets." />
