            <node id="132" label="init-system-helpers">
                <attvalues>
                    <attvalue for="0" value="helper tools for all init systems" />
                    <attvalue for="1" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="2" value='helper tools for all init systems&#10; This package contains helper tools that are necessary for switching between&#10; the various init systems that Debian contains (e. g. sysvinit or&#10; systemd). An example is deb-systemd-helper, a script that enables systemd unit&#10; files without depending on a running systemd.&#10; .&#10; It also includes the "service", "invoke-rc.d", and "update-rc.d" scripts which&#10; provide an abstraction for enabling, disabling, starting, and stopping&#10; services for all supported Debian init systems as specified by the policy.&#10; .&#10; While this package is maintained by pkg-systemd-maintainers, it is NOT&#10; specific to systemd at all. Maintainers of other init systems are welcome to&#10; include their helpers in this package.' />
                    <attvalue for="3" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="4" value="133" />
                    <attvalue for="5" value="yes" />
                    <attvalue for="6" value="Ubuntu Developers &lt;ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com&gt;" />
                    <attvalue for="7" value="" />
