            <node id="203" label="libcurl3t64-gnutls:amd64">
                <attvalues>
                    <attvalue for="0" value="easy-to-use client-side URL transfer library (GnuTLS flavour)" />
                    <attvalue for="1" value='[[{"name": "libcurl3-gnutls", "op": "&lt;&lt;", "version": "8.18.0-1ubuntu2.1"}]]' />
                    <attvalue for="2" value="easy-to-use client-side URL transfer library (GnuTLS flavour)&#10; libcurl is an easy-to-use client-side URL transfer library, supporting DICT,&#10; FILE, FTP, FTPS, GOPHER, HTTP, HTTPS, IMAP, IMAPS, LDAP, LDAPS, POP3, POP3S,&#10; RTMP, RTSP, SCP, SFTP, SMTP, SMTPS, TELNET and TFTP.&#10; .&#10; libcurl supports SSL certificates, HTTP POST, HTTP PUT, FTP uploading, HTTP&#10; form based upload, proxies, cookies, user+password authentication (Basic,&#10; Digest, NTLM, Negotiate, Kerberos), file transfer resume, http proxy tunneling&#10; and more!&#10; .&#10; libcurl is free, thread-safe, IPv6 compatible, feature rich, well supported,&#10; fast, thoroughly documented and is already used by many known, big and&#10; successful companies and numerous applications.&#10; .&#10; SSL support is provided by GnuTLS." />
                    <attvalue for="3" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="4" value="993" />
                    <attvalue for="5" value="no" />
                    <attvalue for="6" value="Ubuntu Developers &lt;ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com&gt;" />
                    <attvalue for="7" value="" />
