            <node id="210" label="libdeflate0:amd64">
                <attvalues>
                    <attvalue for="0" value="fast, whole-buffer DEFLATE-based compression and decompression" />
                    <attvalue for="1" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="2" value="fast, whole-buffer DEFLATE-based compression and decompression&#10; The supported formats are:&#10;  * DEFLATE (raw)&#10;  * zlib (a.k.a. DEFLATE with a zlib wrapper)&#10;  * gzip (a.k.a. DEFLATE with a gzip wrapper)&#10; .&#10; libdeflate is heavily optimized. It is significantly faster than the zlib&#10; library, both for compression and decompression, and especially on x86&#10; processors. In addition, libdeflate provides optional high compression modes&#10; that provide a better compression ratio than the zlib's &quot;level 9&quot;." />
                    <attvalue for="3" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="4" value="107" />
                    <attvalue for="5" value="no" />
                    <attvalue for="6" value="Ubuntu Developers &lt;ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com&gt;" />
                    <attvalue for="7" value="" />
