                    <attvalue for="1" value='[[{"name": "libgdbm-compat4", "op": "&lt;&lt;", "version": "1.26-1build1"}]]' />
                    <attvalue for="2" value="GNU dbm database routines (legacy support runtime version) &#10; GNU dbm ('gdbm') is a library of database functions that use extendible&#10; hashing and works similarly to the standard UNIX 'dbm' functions.&#10; .&#10; The basic use of 'gdbm' is to store key/data pairs in a data file, thus&#10; providing a persistent version of the 'dictionary' Abstract Data Type&#10; ('hash' to perl programmers).&#10; This package includes library files, required to run old programs,&#10; that use legacy 'dbm' interface. For new programs, please use modern&#10; interface, provided by libgdbm6t64 and libgdbm-dev." />
                    <attvalue for="3" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="4" value="35" />
