            <node id="350" label="libpango-1.0-0:amd64">
                <attvalues>
                    <attvalue for="0" value="Layout and rendering of internationalized text" />
                    <attvalue for="1" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="2" value="Layout and rendering of internationalized text&#10; Pango is a library for layout and rendering of text, with an emphasis&#10; on internationalization. Pango can be used anywhere that text layout is&#10; needed. however, most of the work on Pango-1.0 was done using the GTK+&#10; widget toolkit as a test platform. Pango forms the core of text and&#10; font handling for GTK+-2.0.&#10; .&#10; Pango is designed to be modular; the core Pango layout can be used with&#10; four different font backends:&#10;  - Core X windowing system fonts&#10;  - Client-side fonts on X using the Xft library&#10;  - Direct rendering of scalable fonts using the FreeType library&#10;  - Native fonts on Microsoft backends&#10; .&#10; This package contains the shared libraries." />
                    <attvalue for="3" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="4" value="556" />
                    <attvalue for="5" value="no" />
                    <attvalue for="6" value="Ubuntu Developers &lt;ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com&gt;" />
                    <attvalue for="7" value="" />
                    <attvalue for="8" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="9" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="10" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="11" value="libs" />
                    <attvalue for="12" value="pango1.0" />
                    <attvalue for="13" value="1.57.0-1" />
                    <attvalue for="14" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="15" value="1.57.0-1" />
                </attvalues>
                </node>
