            <node id="457" label="libxrender1:amd64">
                <attvalues>
                    <attvalue for="0" value="X Rendering Extension client library" />
                    <attvalue for="1" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="2" value="X Rendering Extension client library&#10; The X Rendering Extension (Render) introduces digital image composition as&#10; the foundation of a new rendering model within the X Window System.&#10; Rendering geometric figures is accomplished by client-side tessellation into&#10; either triangles or trapezoids.  Text is drawn by loading glyphs into the&#10; server and rendering sets of them.  The Xrender library exposes this&#10; extension to X clients.&#10; .&#10; More information about X.Org can be found at:&#10; &lt;URL:https://www.X.org&gt;&#10; .&#10; This module can be found at&#10; git://anongit.freedesktop.org/git/xorg/lib/libXrender" />
                    <attvalue for="3" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="4" value="58" />
                    <attvalue for="5" value="no" />
                    <attvalue for="6" value="Ubuntu Developers &lt;ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com&gt;" />
