                <attvalues>
                    <attvalue for="0" value="Linux Standard Base version reporting utility (minimal implementation)" />
                    <attvalue for="1" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="2" value="Linux Standard Base version reporting utility (minimal implementation)&#10; The Linux Standard Base (http://www.linuxbase.org/) is a standard&#10; core system that third-party applications written for Linux can&#10; depend upon.&#10; .&#10; The lsb_release command is a simple tool to help identify the Linux&#10; distribution being used and its compliance with the Linux Standard Base.&#10; .&#10; This package contains a bare-bones implementation that uses the&#10; information in /etc/os-release instead of relying on LSB packages." />
                    <attvalue for="3" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="4" value="18" />
