                    <attvalue for="0" value="Pattern scanning and text processing language" />
                    <attvalue for="1" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="2" value="Pattern scanning and text processing language&#10; Mawk is an interpreter for the AWK Programming Language. The AWK&#10; language is useful for manipulation of data files, text retrieval and&#10; processing, and for prototyping and experimenting with algorithms. Mawk&#10; is a new awk meaning it implements the AWK language as defined in Aho,&#10; Kernighan and Weinberger, The AWK Programming Language, Addison-Wesley&#10; Publishing, 1988. (Hereafter referred to as the AWK book.) Mawk conforms&#10; to the POSIX 1003.2 (draft 11.3) definition of the AWK language&#10; which contains a few features not described in the AWK book, and mawk&#10; provides a small number of extensions.&#10; .&#10; Mawk is smaller and much faster than gawk. It has some compile-time&#10; limits such as NF = 32767 and sprintf buffer = 1020." />
                    <attvalue for="3" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="4" value="286" />
                    <attvalue for="5" value="no" />
                    <attvalue for="6" value="Ubuntu Developers &lt;ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com&gt;" />
