                <attvalues>
                    <attvalue for="0" value="/proc file system utilities" />
                    <attvalue for="1" value='[[{"name": "manpages-de", "op": "&lt;&lt;", "version": "4.9.1-2"}], [{"name": "manpages-fr", "op": "&lt;&lt;", "version": "4.9.1-2"}], [{"name": "manpages-fr-extra", "op": "&lt;&lt;", "version": "20151231+nmu1"}], [{"name": "manpages-pl", "op": "&lt;&lt;", "version": "1:4.9.1-2"}]]' />
                    <attvalue for="2" value='/proc file system utilities&#10; This package provides command line and full screen utilities for browsing&#10; procfs, a "pseudo" file system dynamically generated by the kernel to&#10; provide information about the status of entries in its process table&#10; (such as whether the process is running, stopped, or a "zombie").&#10; .&#10; It contains free, kill, pkill, pgrep, pmap, ps, pwdx, skill, slabtop,&#10; snice, sysctl, tload, top, uptime, vmstat, w, and watch.' />
