            <node id="531" label="python3-argcomplete">
                <attvalues>
                    <attvalue for="0" value="bash/zsh tab completion for argparse (for Python 3)" />
                    <attvalue for="1" value='[[{"name": "python-argcomplete", "op": null, "version": null}]]' />
                    <attvalue for="2" value="bash/zsh tab completion for argparse (for Python 3)&#10; Argcomplete provides easy, extensible command line tab completion of&#10; arguments for your Python script.&#10; .&#10; It makes two assumptions:&#10; .&#10;  * You're using bash or zsh as your shell&#10;  * You're using argparse to manage your command line arguments/options&#10; .&#10; Argcomplete is particularly useful if your program has lots of&#10; options or subparsers, and if your program can dynamically suggest&#10; completions for your argument/option values (for example, if the user&#10; is browsing resources over the network).&#10; .&#10; This package provides the module for Python 3.x." />
                    <attvalue for="3" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="4" value="163" />
                    <attvalue for="5" value="no" />
                    <attvalue for="6" value="Ubuntu Developers &lt;ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com&gt;" />
                    <attvalue for="7" value="" />
