            <node id="552" label="python3-gdbm">
                <attvalues>
                    <attvalue for="0" value="package depending on all supported Python 3 gdbm modules" />
                    <attvalue for="1" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="2" value="package depending on all supported Python 3 gdbm modules&#10; GNU dbm database module for Python 3.x. Install this if you want to&#10; create or read GNU dbm database files with Python. Debian breaks out the gdbm&#10; module from the Python standard library to reduce the dependency footprint.&#10; .&#10; The package currently depends on python3.14-gdbm. In the&#10; future, dependencies on jython (Python for a JVM) and ironpython (Python for&#10; Mono) may be added.&#10; .&#10; Note that this package will not force the installation of all supported Python&#10; interpreters, it only makes sure that the modules are available." />
                    <attvalue for="3" value="[]" />
