            <node id="660" label="squashfs-tools">
                <attvalues>
                    <attvalue for="0" value="Tool to create and append to squashfs filesystems" />
                    <attvalue for="1" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="2" value="Tool to create and append to squashfs filesystems&#10; Squashfs is a highly compressed read-only filesystem for Linux. It uses zlib&#10; compression to compress both files, inodes and directories. Inodes in the&#10; system are very small and all blocks are packed to minimise data overhead.&#10; Block sizes greater than 4K are supported up to a maximum of 64K.&#10; .&#10; Squashfs is intended for general read-only filesystem use, for archival use&#10; (i.e. in cases where a .tar.gz file may be used), and in constrained block&#10; device/memory systems (e.g. embedded systems) where low overhead is needed." />
                    <attvalue for="3" value="[]" />
                    <attvalue for="4" value="599" />
                    <attvalue for="5" value="no" />
                    <attvalue for="6" value="Ubuntu Developers &lt;ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com&gt;" />
                    <attvalue for="7" value="" />
